            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you kindly link to SMBPBI spec.\n\nI did a quick search but could not find any document directly."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "SMPBI is not a publish specification unfortunately (similar to PECI, and other proprietary OOB interfaces)"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can we note that down in the commit message and\nin the schema 'description'.\n\nSomething like\n\n`'SMBPBI' is a closed nvidia specification`\n\nThen it will be clear that it's not something anyone can simply edit and refactor."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "> Then it will be clear that it's not something anyone can simply edit and refactor.\n\nThat's not the intent, and anyone that has the hardware and an incentive to test can refactor as needed.  If we're going to start requiring a specification for all interfaces, I don't think the project can succeed.\n\nBut yes, I've updated the description."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/smbpbi.json",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "specifying poll rate in seconds sounds limiting, can we make it milliseconds?\n\nJust asking, not familiar SMBPBI spec."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/smbpbi.json",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aushim Nagarkatti",
                        "email": "aush281@gmail.com",
                        "username": "aushimnagarkatti"
                    },
                    "message": "seconds is accurate per spec. For context, the sensor polls readings from a virtual eeprom over i2c."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/smbpbi.json",
                    "line": 27,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/smbpbi.json",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Can you reference the threshold schema like this:\n```\"$ref\": \"#/$defs/Types/Thresholds\"```\n\nor is there something specific about this one which makes it different.\n\nSame for some of the other properties, they might already have schema definitions."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/smbpbi.json",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aushim Nagarkatti",
                        "email": "aush281@gmail.com",
                        "username": "aushimnagarkatti"
                    },
                    "message": "Done, looks like I had to reference these properties in the legacy schema, please let me know if that needs to change."
                },
                {
                    "file": "schemas/smbpbi.json",
                    "line": 45,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "I have a patch for that https://gerrit.openbmc.org/c/openbmc/entity-manager/+/81553\n\nsince these common schemas are used in new schema development, they can be split from the legacy sensor schemas.\n\nLooks like your schema is using these standard definitions now so it looks ok to me from that perspective. Thanks!"
                }
            ],
